diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..24ddbd6 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,17 +1,13 @@
-# The DevTools Times
+# smallpt browser playground
 
-This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
+Kevin Beason’s MIT-licensed [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/) C++ path tracer, compiled to WebAssembly with Emscripten 4.0.19. The home page is prerendered to `dist/client/index.html`; rendering runs entirely on the client in a module Web Worker.
 
+Install dependencies with `pnpm install`, then run `pnpm build`. The compiled `.wasm` and JavaScript loader are checked into `public/wasm/`, so normal app builds do not need Emscripten. The app retains its existing Astro Node adapter for the other routes.
 
-```sh
-pnpm install && pnpm run start
-```
+To rebuild WebAssembly, activate Emscripten 4.0.19 and run `pnpm build:wasm` (or set `EMXX` to the path to `em++`). Serve the built app over HTTP with `.wasm` support; browsers do not support module workers from `file://` pages.
 
-The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
+`vendor/smallpt/original.cpp` is the original source, with its license alongside it. `browser.cpp` retains the original integrator and scene and replaces the command-line entry point with a progressive RGBA buffer interface. Each pass traces four samples per pixel, averages linear radiance, and gamma-corrects the display buffer. The worker copies each frame before transferring it to the canvas. No OpenMP, cross-origin isolation, GPU, or backend rendering is required.
 
-## Tech Stack
+The page starts rendering automatically. Randomize colors changes the two side walls and the mirror and glass spheres, then starts a new render. Resolution and sample controls restart rendering; pause/resume keeps accumulated samples. Download saves the current frame as PNG. `public/render-preview.png` is a 256-sample native render from the same C++ adaptation, shown until the first live frame arrives.
 
-- **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
-- **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
-- **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
-- **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+Validation: the production Astro build and a Node WebAssembly smoke check verifying non-black opaque RGBA output and changed pixels after changing sphere colors. No browser verification or preview server was used.
